# Directory operations & streams of files

`Files` exposes directories as **streams of `Path`** — the whole module-07 toolkit applies.

## `Files.list` — one level deep

```java
try (Stream<Path> entries = Files.list(dir)) {
    entries.filter(Files::isRegularFile)
           .map(Path::getFileName).sorted().forEach(...);
}
```

## `Files.walk` — the whole tree, recursively

```java
try (Stream<Path> tree = Files.walk(start)) {
    long n = tree.filter(p -> p.toString().endsWith(".java")).count();
}   // Files.walk(start, 2) bounds the depth
```

## `Files.find` — walk + built-in filter

```java
Files.find(start, Integer.MAX_VALUE,
    (p, attrs) -> attrs.isRegularFile() && attrs.size() > 1_000_000)
```

## The rule you cannot forget

Every `Files` stream (`list`/`walk`/`find`) holds an **open OS handle** → **always** a try-with-resources. (In-memory `list.stream()` doesn't — only file-backed sources do.)
